  "title": "Eid",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bangladesh celebrates two Eids: **ঈদুল ফিতর** at the end of Ramadan and **ঈদুল আজহা** (the festival of sacrifice). The greeting for both is **ঈদ মোবারক!** — reply with the same.\n\nEid morning: men go to the Eid prayer (**ঈদের নামাজ**), everyone wears **নতুন** (new) clothes, and homes serve **সেমাই**. Children bow to elders and receive **সালামি** — Eid money. **আপু, সালামি দাও!** is a classic line from a younger sibling.\n\nGrammar: **ঈদে** = 'at Eid' (locative), **ঈদের** = 'of Eid' (genitive): **ঈদের দিন** 'on Eid day'.\n\nMillions leave Dhaka for their village homes at Eid — the city goes quiet for days.",
